{
  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.635 acc / 0.618 F1 at 7.02 GPU hours. With only one data point, the most critical uncertainty is whether the expensive ViT-L image encoder is actually necessary or whether a cheaper ResNet50 backbone would yield comparable accuracy. Question tested: config_036 changes exactly one variable from config_004 (imagenet_vit_l → resnet50), holding all other settings identical (pca_n2000, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile, multimodal). This clean ablation isolates the image-encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) If ResNet50 matches or nearly matches ViT-L accuracy, every subsequent multimodal experiment becomes ~40-50% cheaper, freeing GPU budget for more informative experiments within the 8 remaining slots. (2) If ResNet50 is clearly worse, we confirm ViT-L is essential and can focus remaining budget on RNA-encoder and aggregation choices. (3) The cost/accuracy tradeoff of the image backbone is the highest-leverage design decision for the rest of the search because it affects the cost of all future multimodal runs. Expected relative cost: ~3-4 GPU hours (roughly 50-55% of config_004's 7.02), since ResNet50 (~25M params) is substantially smaller than ViT-L (~300M params) while the RNA and aggregation pipelines remain the same."
}

